<h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
<p>This policy explains how content on this platform is produced, labeled, and corrected.
It exists so readers can judge what kind of information they are looking at.</p>
<h2>Content types and labels</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Community experience records</strong> are de-identified, editorially
  rewritten summaries of publicly shared recovery accounts. They are labeled as community
  reports. They are <em>never</em> presented as scientific evidence.</li>
  <li><strong>Community patterns</strong> are recurring structures observed across multiple
  experience records. They are observations, not findings.</li>
  <li><strong>Synthetic examples</strong> (used only to demonstrate the data model) are
  explicitly labeled SYNTHETIC everywhere they appear. They are excluded from all
  statistics, never cited as real experiences, and never used as evidence.</li>
  <li><strong>Research summaries</strong> paraphrase published studies with source type and
  evidence strength ratings. Where DOIs or PMIDs are known they are provided; where
  uncertain, they are left unstated rather than guessed.</li>
  <li><strong>Claims and controversies</strong> present the state of the evidence with
  explicit status ratings and named uncertainties.</li>
</ul>
<h2>De-identification and privacy</h2>
<p>Community-derived records are processed to remove usernames, identifiers, contact
details, locations, and other personal information. Source material is never published
and is excluded from the public repository. Do not attempt to re-identify records.</p>
<h2>Language and tone</h2>
<p>Content is written to be calm, non-judgmental, and evidence-aware. It does not shame
pornography users, does not assume every reader has an addiction, and does not diagnose.</p>
<h2>Evidence boundaries</h2>
<p>The platform maintains a strict separation: personal experience is not evidence,
community observation is not causation, correlation is not causation, and "uncertain" is
not "false." Statements that exceed available evidence are corrected or removed.</p>
<h2>Corrections</h2>
<p>Factual errors are corrected when identified, including errors in published analysis
pieces. The current version of any page is authoritative.</p>
<p>Last updated: 2026-10-04.</p>

</BaseLayout>
